{
	"FileVersion": 3,
	"Version": 1,
	"VersionName": "1.0.0",
	"EngineVersion": "5.8.0",
	"FriendlyName": "TurretMind - Target Acquisition on a Budget",
	"Description": "One targeting service for hundreds of turrets instead of a copy of the same logic inside every turret. Targets live in a uniform grid, not in a list every turret walks, so a turret only ever looks at the cells inside its own range. Re-evaluation runs round-robin under a hard per-frame budget, line-of-sight traces are spread over frames and cached, and a turret keeps its target until its turn comes round again - nothing ever stalls. Hysteresis stops turrets flickering between two equally good targets, and lead prediction hands you the point to aim at instead of the point the target is standing on. TurretMind does not shoot: no projectiles, no damage, no hit detection. It decides what is aimed at and where to lead - the rest stays yours.",
	"Category": "AI",
	"CreatedBy": "Silvan Teufel",
	"CreatedByURL": "https://silvan.teufel-engineering.com",
	"DocsURL": "https://github.com/SimulatedFlow/ue-plugin-TurretMind",
